the Trump administration meanwhile  blasting China for its handling of the  outbreak President Trump saying Beijing  made a huge mistake as you just heard  trying to cover up the crisis Secretary  of State Mike Pompeo also ripping China  for suppressing important information  we've seen the fact that they kicked two  journalists out we saw the fact that  those who were trying to report on this  medical professionals inside of China  were silenced they shut down reporting  all the kind of things that  authoritarian regimes do it's the way  God made his party's opera this is  classic communist disinformation effort  that created enormous risk  let's bring in Fox News contributor  Byron York he is also the chief  political correspondent for the  Washington Examiner he joins us now  Byron good morning to you  so we'll get to the president's reaction  last night in just a moment but first  Mike Pompeo blasting China in that  brand-new interview well remember  Pompeyo is a former CIA director so he  knows intelligence he knows Chinese  tactics not only in the virus but in  years past so this is something that he  has some expertise to talk about US  officials apparently now believe that  China hid or destroyed evidence to keep  the severity of this crisis a secret  from the the world this is something  that US officials have noticed for a  while  a senator not too long ago told me that  back in January he was noticing the  discrepancy between Chinese government  public statements everything's fine  nothing to see here  and the increasingly draconian efforts  they were taking to contain the virus in  Wuhan that may you know his is his  eyebrows go up and and be suspicious of  what was going on so US officials have  been looking at something funky going on  in China for quite a while  interesting what was your takeaway then  from the president's words last night as  you just heard him say he believes that  China made a huge mistake and he has in  the past vowed retaliation what does  that tell you about the u.s. next move  when it comes to China well first of all  the idea is is not that it was done  deliberately it was not created as a  bio-weapon or something like that but  that china was studying this virus in  part apparently to show that it had a  world-class biology capability and that  by accident it got out of the laboratory  so the question is what does the united  states do now the president has had a  very delicate relationship with China  over his entire presidency as he tries  to get increased and better for the US  trade terms with China there are obvious  things to do I mean the United States  has funded the virology lab in Wuhan  maybe that's not a great idea certainly  members of Congress are a lot of members  of Congress who want to stop doing that  so I think there'll be a number of  actions the the administration will take  they may be kind of ascending actions  starting slow and if China does not fix  things or come clean  perhaps they become more serious in  members of Congress stepping forward  with some ideas as well senator Ted Cruz  of Texas talking about the some of the  bills that he's bringing forward to  combat China here's the senator this  week I've got four pieces of legislation  I'm introducing one of them is  legislation that prohibits the u.s.  government from conducting any business  over any telecom or Internet  infrastructure that china owns or  controls why because they use it to  steal that is part of their strategy  it's a bottom line Byron for the  American people sitting at home they  hear the president in that Town Hall  last night talking about a huge mistake  that led to all this on the part of  China  Pompeyo calling it classic communist  disinformation effort the American  people want to know if China will  ultimately be held accountable final  thoughts well as senator Cruz just said  there are a number of members of  Congress who want to do that not clear  what the president will do I mean  there's there's so many different public  concerns about this obviously the first  concern is the health of the American  people and stopping the spread of the  virus the second concern is reopening  the economy I would have to say  the you know taking action against China  is probably the third concern but  absolutely necessary once we find out  what actually happened byron york always  good to talk to you thanks for kicking  off our monday morning show Thank You  Sandra

